2d8-b154-215a4d77456a" :question/math-academy-id "q-282145" :question/problem "Let $a=-6i+3j+2k$ and $b=4i-j+5k.$ Find $a\\times b.$\n\n$a\\times b=$\n\n{{field-1}}$\\,i\\,+\\,$\n{{field-2}}$\\,j\\,-\\,$\n{{field-3}}$\\,k$" :question/worked-solution "Using the determinant formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\times b & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ -6 & 3 & 2 \\\\ 4 & -1 & 5\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}3 & 2 \\\\ -1 & 5\\end{aligned}|i-|\\begin{aligned}-6 & 2 \\\\ 4 & 5\\end{aligned}|j+|\\begin{aligned}-6 & 3 \\\\ 4 & -1\\end{aligned}|k \\\\  & =(3\\cdot 5-2\\cdot -1)i-(-6\\cdot 5-2\\cdot 4)j+(-6\\cdot -1-3\\cdot 4)k \\\\  & =(15+2)i-(-30-8)j+(6-12)k \\\\  & =17\\,i+38\\,j-6\\,k\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-282145/field-1" "q-282145/field-2" "q-282145/field-3"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "733eab11-2a26-5402-8df5-bba50c9beaf9"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-282145"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]}]
